<title>CANADA: Stelco pipe unit workers go on strike.</title>
<headline>Stelco pipe unit workers go on strike.</headline>
<dateline>WELLAND, Ontario 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stelpipe Ltd, a wholly owned subsidiary of Stelco Inc said its unionised workers went on strike Friday.</p>
<p>The steel pipe and tubing maker said members of the Canadian Auto Workers (CAW) union local 523 went on strike after the two sides failed to reach a new labor agreement.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
